Subject: [PATCH] unixfdsrc: register reference timestamp meta before receiving

GstReferenceTimestampMeta is serialized by a producer even if no local
consumer has registered it yet. Register the core meta in the receiver
before deserializing the first frame, retaining timestamps from startup.

--- a/gst/unixfd/gstunixfdsrc.c
+++ b/gst/unixfd/gstunixfdsrc.c
@@ -128,6 +128,10 @@
 gst_unix_fd_src_init (GstUnixFdSrc * self)
 {
   g_return_if_fail (GST_IS_UNIX_FD_SRC (self));
+
+  /* Core metadata is registered lazily. Deserialization looks up its name
+   * before downstream RTP elements have had a chance to use the type. */
+  gst_reference_timestamp_meta_get_info ();

   self->cancellable = g_cancellable_new ();
   self->memories = g_hash_table_new (NULL, NULL);
